# GLASSPOCKET / Build Spec Section 04B
#
# RULE: no secret is ever committed, printed to a log, pasted into a
# Streamlit page, or visible in the demo recording. These entries exist
# BEFORE the first commit, not after. If a key is ever exposed, rotate it
# and note the rotation in the README rather than quietly rewriting history.

# THE WRITING SYSTEM. Never commit any of this.
#
# algorithm_blog/ holds the DEV.to ranking manual, the Forem pre-flight
# script and its pinned baseline, the post template, the two prior posts
# that won, and every draft written from them. The directory entry alone
# is enough; the patterns under it are belt and braces so a draft that
# gets moved out of the directory is still refused.
algorithm_blog/
algorithm_blog/**
AGENTS.md
POST-TEMPLATE.md
.forem-baseline
forem-algo-check.sh
FERVOR.md
TELLTAIL.md
*-POST.md
*-DRAFT.md
draft*.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
keys/
*.p8
*.pem
*.key
authority.json
*keypair*.json

# large source data, downloaded by the operator, never committed
data/irs/
data/geo/
data/synthetic/
data/*.duckdb
data/*.parquet
*.csv

# The generated app/assets/geist.css is committed, and so are the four
# woff2 faces plus the variable face it is built from: 264 KB total, and
# it makes tools/build_font_css.py reproducible without reaching npm.
fonts/*.ttf

# node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
dist/

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# os and editors
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# working scratch
spec.txt
